  "result": "I fixed it in `notify()` in `src/server/services/notification-service.ts`. It now skips any recipient whose ID matches `payload.actorId`. I haven't run the test suite.\n\nThe recipient loop had no check for the actor. The `comment.created` handler builds the watcher list from the issue's author and assignee, so a comment from either of them notified the commenter too.\n\nBecause the check sits in `notify()`, it also covers the mention and assignment handlers. `tests/services/notification-service.test.ts` has a case, \"does not notify the actor about their own action\", that expects this behaviour from `notify` itself.\n\nBecause `notify` skips the actor for every kind, self-assignment and self-mention no longer produce a notification either. The `member.joined` case is unaffected in practice: the recipient there is the org owner, and the event's actor is the user who joined.",
